6 | Operational Workflow & Change Control

Everything from here defines how the work should happen, not just what to build.
Think of it as the playbook that locks in your dev philosophy and guardrails.

6.1 Branch & Commit Strategy

Main rule: Never code directly in main.

Branch pattern:

feature/<scope>-<shortdesc>
fix/<issue>-<shortdesc>
refactor/<module>
release/v<version>


Commit format:

[batch] <area>: <action>


Examples:

[batch1] core: implement runtimeManager
[batch3] renderer: wire CanvasPane and RuntimeContext
[batch6] plugins: add schema validation


Each batch corresponds to a milestone in MASTER_TODO.md.

When a batch completes:

Test all flows.

Merge to main with tag: v<major>.<minor>-b<batch#>
Example: v1.0-b4

6.2 Build Commands

The project uses Vite + Electron + Node backends.

Action	Command
Dev start	npm run dev
Build app	npm run build
Lint	npm run lint
Test runtimes	npm run test:runtimes
Package Electron app	npm run package

Custom commands live in /scripts/ (to be added).
Example:

node scripts/runRuntimeTest.js --lang python

6.3 Testing Workflow
Unit tests

Framework: Vitest or Jest.

Focus areas:

sandbox execution

runtime dispatch

aiService error handling

Integration tests

Mock Gemini and OpenAI with local stubs.

Validate model fallback order.

Check runtime logs for correct state transitions.

UI tests

Framework: Playwright.

Test scenarios:

Run code → output visible.

Runtime switch persists.

Plugin load/unload doesn’t crash app.

6.4 Handoff Testing Steps (for AI assistants)

Whenever a new AI instance continues development, it should:

Load this guide (MASTER_BUILD_GUIDE.md) into memory.

Scan existing files to confirm folder integrity matches the layout map.

Compare file headers — any missing or truncated header signals corruption.

Run npm run lint — ensure syntax validity before touching logic.

Backup everything into /sandbox/replace_test/ before overwrite.

Only modify full files (never patch-line insertions).

Log all changes into /docs/CHANGELOG.md under its batch.

6.5 Error Recovery Protocol

If runtime or AI models fail:

Check /logs/runtime_logs/last.log.

Compare with /core/audit.js for timestamp correlation.

If sandbox isolation fails, rollback to last working adapter from /sandbox/replace_test/.

Autorepair Logic (AI use only):

If a function signature mismatch is detected between modules, regenerate the caller, not the callee.

Always preserve manual overrides marked with:

// DOC_MANUAL_OVERRIDE_START
...
// DOC_MANUAL_OVERRIDE_END

6.6 Versioning & Release

Version schema: major.minor.patch-batch

Example: 1.2.0-b5

Each batch must produce a release artifact in /builds/.

When a batch is marked complete:

Tag commit.

Export logs/ai_usage.log and runtime_logs/ as .zip.

Push build notes to /docs/REPORTS.md.

6.7 Configuration Management

Primary Config File: /config/settings.json
Contains:

{
  "theme": "dark",
  "defaultRuntime": "node",
  "autoSave": true,
  "keys": {
    "GEMINI_API_KEY": "...",
    "OPENAI_API_KEY": "..."
  }
}


All config updates should pass through SettingsContext.tsx and core/aiService.js.
Never directly read/write JSON from renderer.

6.8 Logging & Alerts
Type	File	Trigger
AI usage	/logs/ai_usage.log	Every generate() call
Runtime	/logs/runtime_logs/*.json	Each execution
Cache	/logs/model_cache.json	AI response caching
Alerts	/core/alerts.js	error(), warn(), info()
Reports	/docs/REPORTS.md	batch summaries

Alert Levels:

info("runtime started", "runtime")
warn("timeout exceeded", "sandbox")
error("execution crash", "runtime")

6.9 Collaboration Protocol (for multi-AI or human+AI)

When multiple devs or AI workers are coding:

Assign batches, never files.

Always merge completed batches to /sandbox/merge_staging/.

Run diff check → only commit if 100% tested.

Each participant logs summary to /docs/DEV_LOG.md:

Date: 2025-10-19
Batch: 3
Files: CanvasPane.tsx, RuntimeContext.tsx
Changes: Implemented runtime state + console feed.

6.10 Shutdown & Resume Logic

Before halting work:

Run npm run export:state (to snapshot configs + logs).

Zip /sandbox/replace_test/ + /logs/ → store under /archive/auto/.

Update MASTER_TODO.md progress marks.

Commit message:

savepoint: batch <n> – partial progress checkpoint


When resuming:

Extract from latest /archive/auto/*.zip.

Compare guide’s folder map with actual FS before starting.


7 | Visual & UX Stylebook
7.1 Core Design Principles

Minimal noise, maximum focus.
The editor should feel like a workspace, not a product ad.

Readable at 2AM.
Typography and contrast take priority over color “pop.”

Motion with purpose.
Animations must communicate state — not distract.

Symmetry where possible.
Avoid asymmetrical paddings, uneven borders, or inconsistent icon sizing.

Clarity over cleverness.
Every icon and color should mean something; don’t hide behavior in flair.

7.2 Color System

Colors are defined in renderer/styles/theme.css and imported via Tailwind config.

Role	Light Theme	Dark Theme
Primary	#2563EB (blue-600)	#3B82F6 (blue-500)
Accent	#A855F7 (violet-500)	#C084FC (violet-400)
Background	#F9FAFB	#0D1117
Panel	#FFFFFF	#161B22
Border	#E5E7EB	#2D333B
Text (main)	#111827	#F9FAFB
Text (muted)	#6B7280	#9CA3AF
Error	#DC2626	#F87171
Success	#16A34A	#4ADE80
Warning	#F59E0B	#FBBF24

Each token is used through Tailwind’s --tw-color-<role> variable mapping.

7.3 Typography

Font stack:

Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif


Monospace areas:

JetBrains Mono, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace


Scale:

h1 = 1.75rem
h2 = 1.5rem
h3 = 1.25rem
body = 1rem
small = 0.875rem
code = 0.9375rem


Weight: Regular (400), Medium (500), Bold (700)

Use font-medium for UI text, font-bold only for headings or section titles.

7.4 Layout System

All major views (CanvasPane, BrowserPane, ReportsPane, etc.) follow this grid:

-------------------------------------------------------
| Sidebar (60px) |  Main Content (auto)  |  Right Pane |
-------------------------------------------------------


Sidebar: icons only (e.g., run, stop, AI chat, settings)

Right Pane: collapsible drawers for logs, AI feedback, and settings.

Minimum width: 1024px

Max width for text: 900px

Responsive breakpoints (Tailwind defaults):

sm: 640px
md: 768px
lg: 1024px
xl: 1280px
2xl: 1536px

7.5 Component Rules

Buttons

Default: subtle ghost style

Primary actions (Run, Generate): filled with accent color

Destructive: red outline + hover fill

Panels

Each major panel (.pane) should have:

border: 1px solid var(--tw-color-border);
border-radius: 8px;
background: var(--tw-color-panel);


Inputs

Rounded corners: 6px

Focus ring: 2px solid var(--tw-color-primary)

Placeholder opacity: 0.6

Tabs

Active tab bold + underline accent

Inactive tab: faded gray text

Smooth slide transition: 0.2s ease-out

7.6 Motion & Transitions

Use CSS transitions for microfeedback only:

transition: all 0.2s ease-in-out;


Motion guidelines:

Type	Duration	Example
Hover	150ms	Button color
Toggle	250ms	Panel open/close
Load-in	400ms	Fade-in of pane
Error pulse	200ms loop	Red flash for invalid input

Disable unnecessary animations in performance mode (settings.performance = "minimal").

7.7 Iconography

Icon source: Heroicons (outline) or Lucide.

Size system:

small: 16px

medium: 20px

large: 24px

All icons use currentColor for fill.

Always wrap SVG icons with an <IconButton> component for accessibility.

7.8 Themes & Preferences

Themes live in /renderer/styles/themes/:

themes/
 ├── light.css
 ├── dark.css
 └── highcontrast.css


SettingsContext.tsx toggles active theme and persists to localStorage:

const { theme, setTheme } = useSettings();


On change:

document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", theme);


Tailwind variables are scoped under:

[data-theme='dark'] {
  --tw-color-bg: #0D1117;
  --tw-color-panel: #161B22;
}

7.9 Panels & Navigation

Top Toolbar

Left: app logo + project title

Center: file path / runtime indicator

Right: Run / Stop / AI / Settings icons

Left Sidebar

Icons for: Files, Console, Browser, AI, Plugins, Settings

Hover tooltip shows label

Active icon: highlighted with accent underline

Right Drawer

AITaskHistoryTray, AIStatusIndicator, and ReportsPane stack vertically

Collapsible with slide-out transition

7.10 Accessibility

WCAG 2.1 AA contrast minimum

All interactive elements keyboard-accessible:

Tab, Enter, Space

Voice command fallback for critical actions

Dynamic aria labels via React hooks

7.11 CSS Organization
renderer/
 ├── index.css
 ├── styles/
 │    ├── base.css
 │    ├── theme.css
 │    ├── layout.css
