All imports go through AssetDrawer.tsx and AssetPreviewPane.tsx.
Supports drag/drop via preload bridge.

7.14 Future Enhancements

Add glassmorphism theme option (backdrop-filter: blur(8px)).

Optional “matrix rain” background in developer mode.

Custom sound effects for code run/stop (toggle in settings).

Auto theme sync with OS (prefers-color-scheme).


8 | AI Integration Blueprint
8.1 Architecture Overview

Goal: make AI a first-class runtime service, not a bolt-on helper.

Renderer (UI)
   ↓ IPC
Preload Bridge (fileBridge / aiBridge)
   ↓
Core (aiService → models → providers)
   ↓
Network (Gemini / OpenAI / Future)


aiService.js — unified API layer; handles key loading, rate limits, and pluggable providers.

models.js — executes requests, logs them, and handles fallbacks.

renderer/context/AIContext.tsx — manages prompt state and results in UI.

renderer/dashboard/AIPanel.tsx — visual interface for prompts, responses, and status indicators.

8.2 Provider Flow

1. Prompt Created → AIContext

User types or voice-dictates prompt.

Context adds entry to history stack (AIFeedbackPanel).

2. Dispatch → aiService.generate()

Context sends payload through preload bridge to core layer.

aiService reads active provider (gemini, openai, auto).

3. Model Selection → models.generate()

Tries primary provider.

If error or timeout, runs fallback chain (Gemini → OpenAI or vice versa).

4. Response → Audit + Cache

Logs into /logs/model_cache.json and /logs/ai_usage.log.

Sends structured object back to renderer.

5. UI Render

AIPanel shows text response.

AITaskHistoryTray archives conversation.

8.3 Extending Providers

New providers can be added without modifying existing code.

import { registerProvider } from './core/aiService.js';

registerProvider('anthropic', async (prompt, opts) => {
 const res = await fetch('https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages', { … });
 return { provider: 'anthropic', text: res.output };
});


The UI automatically lists new providers from the registry.

8.4 Streaming Responses

Implemented through Server-Sent Events (SSE).

aiService.generate() detects if options.stream === true.

Renderer listens for ai:stream events via ipcRenderer.on.

AIPanel displays partial responses as they arrive.

Fallback to buffered mode if provider does not support SSE.

8.5 Voice Integration

Voice commands are routed through core/voice.js → aiService.
Usage flow:

User says “Ask Gemini to optimize this code.”

Speech to text → Prompt → AIContext.

Response spoken back via TTS engine (optional).

Logs go to voice.log.

8.6 Error Handling & Telemetry

Each AI call produces two entries:

File	Purpose
/logs/ai_usage.log	Prompt, provider, duration
/logs/model_cache.json	Recent responses cache

Telemetry summary schema (/docs/REPORTS.md):

{
 "timestamp": "2025-10-19T02:42:00Z",
 "provider": "gemini",
 "model": "1.5-flash",
 "latency": 1520,
 "chars": 184,
 "success": true
}

8.7 Security & Rate Limits

Keys loaded only in aiService.js.

Never exposed to renderer context.

Per-provider rate limit (60 req/min default).

Global queue shared across threads to avoid spikes.

All requests logged with SHA256(prompt) hash only — no raw content.

8.8 UI Integration Hooks

UI events → AI calls mapping:

Component	Event	Action
CommandPalette	Shift + Enter	Send prompt → generate()
AIPanel	Run button	Manual trigger
AIStatusIndicator	Blink yellow	in-progress
AIFeedbackPanel	+ Icon	New entry in history
App.tsx	Ctrl + /	Open AI command bar

All communication flows through AIContext to avoid cross-component state issues.

8.9 Caching & Reuse

getRecentCompletions(limit) returns latest cached results for instant replay.
If prompt hash matches previous call, models.js returns cached output without API hit.
Useful for voice repeats or plugin auto-runs.

8.10 Future Integration Paths
Target	Purpose
Claude / Anthropic	Long-form reasoning tasks
Mistral	Lightweight local inference
LLama / Ollama	Offline mode
Gemini Vision	Image + code analysis
Whisper	Audio → Text transcription
Stable Diffusion	Asset generation

Each to be plugged via registerProvider() with their own auth config.

8.11 Debug Utilities

Run local diagnostics:

npm run test:ai


Outputs to /logs/ai_diagnostics.log:

✅ Gemini: online (234 ms)
✅ OpenAI: online (417 ms)
⚠️ Cache: over limit (25 entries)

8.12 AI Safety Rules (for autonomous modes)

No unverified API calls without explicit approval flag.

No file system writes outside /workspace/.

Sensitive data masking in logs (sha256 for any string > 30 chars).

Always prompt for confirmation before running generated code in sandbox.

8.13 AI Workflow Checkpoints

Before each AI batch merge:

 Run testConnection() for all providers.

 Validate API keys via validateKeys().

 Confirm model names are current.

 Flush model_cache.json if size > 20.

 Compare latencies → choose default provider dynamically.

9 | Runtime System Blueprint
9.1 Concept

Every runtime (language + environment) plugs into a common interface:

RuntimeManager.run(lang, code, options)


Each runtime adapter declares:

{
  id: "python",
  label: "Python 3.12",
  exec: async (code, opts) => {...},
  detect: (fileName) => fileName.endsWith(".py")
}


Adapters live under /core/runtimes/.
RuntimeManager handles scheduling, logging, and stream output to the renderer.

9.2 Execution Layers
Layer	Responsibility
Renderer	Editor UI + console pane
Preload	Safe IPC bridge for run/stop
Core	RuntimeManager + individual adapters
Worker	Executes sandboxed process
Logger	Captures stdout/stderr and telemetry
9.3 Adapters

Example: /core/runtimes/node.js

export default {
  id: "node",
  label: "Node JS",
  exec: async (code, opts) => {
    const {spawn} = await import("child_process");
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      const proc = spawn("node", ["-e", code], {timeout: opts.timeout || 5000});
      let out = "", err = "";
      proc.stdout.on("data", d => out += d);
      proc.stderr.on("data", d => err += d);
      proc.on("close", () => err ? reject(err) : resolve(out));
    });
  },
  detect: f => f.endsWith(".js")
}


Other adapters mirror this:

python.js → calls python3 -c

bash.js → calls bash -c

csharp.js → compiles and runs via dotnet script

wasm.js → runs via WebAssembly runtime

9.4 RuntimeManager

Core orchestrator (/core/runtimeManager.js):

import {logRuntimeEvent} from "./audit.js";
import adapters from "./runtimes/index.js";

export async function run(lang, code, opts = {}) {
  const adapter = adapters[lang];
  if (!adapter) throw new Error(`No runtime for ${lang}`);
  const start = Date.now();
  try {
    const output = await adapter.exec(code, opts);
    logRuntimeEvent(lang, Date.now() - start, true);
    return {ok: true, output};
  } catch (err) {
    logRuntimeEvent(lang, Date.now() - start, false, err.message);
    throw err;
  }
}

9.5 Sandbox & Security

Execution never touches host directly.

Layer	Isolation Method
Node/Python	vm2 or child_process spawn
Browser	Web Worker
Native	Docker container (bridge: /var/run/docker.sock)
Offline	Ollama or WASM runtime

Configurable via /config/runtime.json:

{
  "sandboxMode": "vm2",
  "maxMemoryMB": 256,
  "timeoutMS": 10000
}

9.6 Telemetry

Every run emits:

/logs/runtime_logs/<timestamp>.json


Schema:

{
  "lang": "python",
  "duration": 482,
  "exit": 0,
  "stdout": "...",
  "stderr": ""
}


Used by:

core/report.js to aggregate daily stats

Dashboard pane for “Recent Runs”

9.7 UI Integration

Renderer components:

Component	Purpose
LiveEditor.tsx	Code editing + run hook
ConsolePane.tsx	Displays stdout/stderr
RuntimeSelector.tsx	Choose language adapter
AssetPreviewPane.tsx	Render image/audio output
AIStatusIndicator.tsx	Blink on AI-assisted run

When user presses Ctrl + Enter:

Editor sends ipcRenderer.send('runtime:run', {lang, code})

Preload bridge calls RuntimeManager.run

Output stream returns to ConsolePane

9.8 Error Feedback

If stderr exists → auto-highlight line numbers in editor.
AI Context can suggest fixes via:

AIContext.requestFix(err.message, codeSnippet)


AIFeedbackPanel then displays “Apply Fix” button.

9.9 Performance Tuning
Metric	Goal
Cold start <	800 ms
Average run	< 3 s
Memory cap	256 MB
Cache hits	> 70%

Enable telemetry dashboard (/renderer/dashboard/PerformancePane.tsx) to visualize runtime latency histograms.

9.10 Extending Runtimes

Add new adapter:

core/runtimes/rust.js


Export id, label, exec, detect.
Update runtimes/index.js to import and register automatically.

9.11 Security Checklist

 No network calls without allowlist

 Sandbox timeouts ≤ 10 s

 No access outside /workspace

