12 | Developer Operations & Deployment Blueprint
12.1 Core Principles

Single Source of Truth: one .env and one /config/settings.json.

Immutable Builds: once packaged, configs load from environment overrides only.

Zero Downtime: hot reload for development, graceful restart for production.

One Command Rule: setup, build, or deploy in one line each.

12.2 Directory Layout
/config/
 ├── settings.json       # API keys, runtime settings, defaults
 ├── email.json          # notifications + SMTP info
 ├── runtime.json        # sandbox configuration
 ├── plugins.json        # plugin toggles
 ├── env.template        # sample .env file
/env/
 ├── .env.local
 ├── .env.production
 └── .env.staging
/scripts/
 ├── setup.js
 ├── build.js
 ├── deploy.js
 ├── test.js
 └── reset.js

12.3 Environment Variables
Variable	Description
GEMINI_API_KEY	Gemini API key
OPENAI_API_KEY	OpenAI API key
NODE_ENV	development / production
PORT	backend port
LOG_LEVEL	debug, info, warn, error
USE_GPU	optional GPU runtime flag
SENTRY_DSN	crash reporting
PLUGINS_PATH	override plugin directory
WORKSPACE_DIR	user workspace path

All .env files are parsed by /scripts/setup.js and validated.

12.4 Local Setup

Command:

npm run setup


/scripts/setup.js

import fs from "fs";
import dotenv from "dotenv";

if (!fs.existsSync(".env")) {
  fs.copyFileSync("./config/env.template", ".env");
  console.log("✔ .env created from template");
}

const env = dotenv.config().parsed;
console.log("Loaded environment:", Object.keys(env));


Creates .env → validates keys → prepares /logs/, /workspace/, /plugins/ if missing.

12.5 Development Workflow
Command	Action
npm run dev	Starts Electron + backend + live reload
npm run dev:server	Backend only
npm run dev:ui	Renderer only
npm run watch	Watches /core and /renderer for hot reload
npm run lint	ESLint and Prettier
npm run test	Unit and integration tests

Local dev spins up:

Backend: Express + WebSocket on port 5050

Frontend: Vite / React dev server on port 3000

Bridge: Electron preload layer connecting both

12.6 Build Pipeline
Step	Description
npm run build:core	Transpile core JS to /dist/core/
npm run build:ui	Builds React app with Vite
npm run build:electron	Bundles Electron main/preload
npm run build	Runs all builds sequentially
npm run package	Creates platform-specific installers

Build output layout:

/dist/
 ├── core/
 ├── renderer/
 ├── preload/
 └── main/

12.7 CI/CD Pipeline

For GitHub Actions or similar:

.github/workflows/build.yml

name: Build & Deploy

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: 20
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run build
      - run: npm test
      - run: npm run package
      - name: Upload Artifact
        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: build
          path: dist/


Deployment variants:

dev → auto-deploy preview build to localhost:5050

staging → pushes Docker image to registry

production → pushes release build + tagged version

