13 | Visual Experience & Theming Blueprint
13.1 Design Philosophy

Function first. No empty decoration; motion must clarify state.

Mood second. A palette that supports long creative sessions — calm neutrals, accent colors for state (blue = thinking, amber = pending, green = done, red = error).

Depth through layering. Panels float with subtle shadows; AI responses glow faintly on hover to suggest “alive.”

Consistency over flash. Everything uses the same 8 px spacing grid.

13.2 CSS Architecture
/renderer/styles/
 ├── variables.css        # color palette + spacing tokens
 ├── base.css             # resets + typography
 ├── components.css       # buttons, inputs, modals, panels
 ├── animations.css       # transitions + keyframes
 ├── themes/
 │    ├── light.css
 │    ├── dark.css
 │    └── solarized.css
 └── index.css            # global import hub


All React components import from index.css.
Scoped class naming follows BEM (panel__header--active).

Use CSS variables (--bg-primary, --text-muted) for theme swaps at runtime.

13.3 Global Variables Example

variables.css

:root {
  --font-sans: "Inter", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  --radius-sm: 4px;
  --radius-md: 8px;
  --radius-lg: 16px;
  --transition-fast: 120ms ease;
  --transition-slow: 280ms ease;
  --shadow-sm: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
  --shadow-md: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);
  --shadow-lg: 0 8px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
}

13.4 Theme Tokens
Token	Light	Dark	Solarized
--bg-primary	#ffffff	#121212	#fdf6e3
--bg-secondary	#f3f3f3	#1e1e1e	#eee8d5
--text-primary	#111	#eee	#657b83
--accent	#3b82f6	#60a5fa	#268bd2
