Theme files (e.g., dark.css) just override these variables.
Switch themes by toggling <body data-theme="dark">.

13.5 Component Styling Guide
Panels
.panel {
  background: var(--bg-secondary);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  transition: box-shadow var(--transition-slow);
}
.panel:hover {
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
}

Buttons
.btn {
  padding: 6px 12px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  transition: background var(--transition-fast);
}
.btn--primary {
  background: var(--accent);
  color: #fff;
}
.btn--primary:hover {
  filter: brightness(1.1);
}

Inputs & Text Areas

Consistent height (36 px).
Focus ring = outline: 2px solid var(--accent);.

13.6 Layout System

12-column grid via CSS Grid.

Breakpoints:

≤ 600px → mobile stack

600–1200px → two-column

≥ 1200px → three-pane desktop

Grid tokens in variables.css:

--gap-sm: 8px;
--gap-md: 16px;
--gap-lg: 24px;

13.7 Animations & Transitions

animations.css

@keyframes fadeIn { from {opacity:0;} to {opacity:1;} }
@keyframes pulse { 0%,100% {opacity:.8;} 50% {opacity:1;} }

.fade-in { animation: fadeIn 0.2s ease both; }
.pulse { animation: pulse 2s infinite ease-in-out; }


Use only motion with purpose — hover feedback, load transitions, AI response arrival.

13.8 Theming Logic in React

/renderer/context/ThemeContext.tsx

import React, { createContext, useState, useEffect } from "react";

export const ThemeContext = createContext({ theme: "light", setTheme: ()=>{} });

export function ThemeProvider({ children }) {
  const [theme, setTheme] = useState(localStorage.getItem("theme") || "light");

  useEffect(() => {
    document.body.dataset.theme = theme;
    localStorage.setItem("theme", theme);
  }, [theme]);

  return (
    <ThemeContext.Provider value={{ theme, setTheme }}>
      {children}
    </ThemeContext.Provider>
  );
}


Switch theme anywhere:

const { theme, setTheme } = useContext(ThemeContext);
<button onClick={() => setTheme(theme === "light" ? "dark" : "light")}>Toggle Theme</button>

