14 | Final Integration Checklist & Handoff Instructions
14.1 Primary Objective

Gemini Playground is a hybrid AI-development environment designed to:

Support multi-model AI orchestration (Gemini, OpenAI, and user plugins).

Run in Electron for desktop or Node/Vite for web.

Be self-replicating and modular — every component can rebuild itself from configuration.

Stay code-first, but with a responsive, reactive UI built for creative workflows.

14.2 Core Principles

Do not delete working systems — only extend or merge them.

Full-file commits only — partial edits cause state drift.

If a file is replaced, mark it clearly in the log.

Every function must preserve original behavior unless deprecated explicitly.

Read from environment before defaults — never hardcode secrets.

Front and back stay decoupled; communicate through WebSocket or API only.

One unified style: all new code follows async/await, ES module syntax, and strong typing in TS files.

14.3 Folder Overview
gemini-playground/
 ├── core/              # backend logic and AI orchestration
 ├── renderer/          # React-based UI
 ├── preload/           # Electron preload bridges
 ├── server/            # Express + WebSocket backend
 ├── plugins/           # user and system extensions
 ├── config/            # runtime and key configuration
 ├── logs/              # runtime, AI, and security logs
 ├── .vscode/           # workspace settings
 ├── .env               # local environment keys
 ├── package.json
 ├── vite.config.js
 └── tsconfig.json


Each subsystem can be run standalone for testing.

14.4 System Dependencies
Type	Description
Node.js	v20 or later
npm	9+
Python (optional)	for code analysis plugins
Electron	bundled automatically
Tailwind	for utility CSS
React 18+	for renderer
Express	for backend API
Socket.io	for live bridge
Vite	for development and build pipeline
14.5 Core Runtime Flow
Electron boot
 └── loads preload/
      ├── bridges IPC + file system
      └── spawns server/index.js

Server startup
 ├── middleware stack → CORS, rateLimit, JSON parsing
 ├── loads core/aiService + core/models
 └── attaches websocket bridge

Renderer startup
 ├── React mount → App.tsx
 ├── loads AIContext, SettingsContext, ProjectsContext
 └── mounts panels (AI, Diff, Plugins, Settings)

PluginManager
 ├── loads /plugins/*.js
 ├── registers custom providers to aiService
 └── emits "plugin:ready"

AIService
 ├── resolves provider (Gemini/OpenAI/plugin)
 ├── sends request
 └── logs + caches result

All components update via context + WebSocket events

14.6 Key Interactions
From	To	Channel	Purpose
Renderer	Core	IPC / WS	Trigger AI request
Core	Renderer	WS	Send AI responses
Renderer	Server	REST	File actions, logs, metrics
Plugin	Core	Direct import	Extend AI or UI logic
14.7 Logging System

/logs/core.log — system events

/logs/audit.log — security and config changes

/logs/ai_usage.log — model call summaries

/logs/plugin.log — plugin load results

/logs/runtime_logs/ — execution results

/logs/metrics/ — daily metrics JSON

All timestamps use UTC ISO 8601.

14.8 Handoff Rules for Next Developer

Full-file discipline

Never copy snippets.

Always commit entire file content.

Include path and LOC in commit log.

Change Log Format

[UPDATE] /core/models.js (312 LOC)
Added: multi-provider retry system.
Replaced: deprecated model switch logic.


Plugin Safety

Each plugin runs sandboxed (vm2 or eval guard).

Must export { name, init, onMessage }.

Log on load to /logs/plugin.log.

AI Provider Expansion

Register new providers via aiService.registerProvider(name, fn).

Never modify base functions directly.

UI Additions

Extend App.tsx routing only via Context or lazy loading.

Reuse CSS tokens from /renderer/styles/variables.css.

Testing

Run npm run test:full before merge.

Include snapshot comparisons for visual regressions.

Error Policy

All thrown errors must bubble to global handler.

No silent catches unless explicitly noted.

14.9 Quick Restore Procedure

If a replacement or update breaks functionality:

git restore path/to/file
npm run clean:cache
npm run dev


If lost entirely:

Recover from /logs/autoBackup/YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM.zip

Re-run scripts/setup.js

14.10 Validation Steps Before Commit
Step	Command
Lint	npm run lint
Typecheck	npm run typecheck
Unit tests	npm run test
Build test	npm run build
UI preview	npm run dev

A change only passes once all succeed.

