14.12 Development Commands Summary
Action	Command
Setup	npm run setup
Dev mode	npm run dev
Dev server only	npm run dev:server
Build	npm run build
Package	npm run dist
Test suite	npm run test
Clean cache	npm run clean
Watch logs	npm run logs:watch
14.13 Emergency Recovery

If config or code corruption detected:

npm run repair


Triggers recovery daemon:

Validates all .json config files

Restores from last good /autoBackup snapshot

Rebuilds dependency graph

Restarts automatically

14.14 Team / AI Collaboration Etiquette

Always start with scan project before edits.

Always confirm file status (new vs replace).

Include full file code in every update.

Do not delete original user logic; wrap or extend it.

Keep commentary minimal but clear (contextual inline comments only).

End each major cycle with confirm and backup snapshot.

14.15 Final Notes

This project was built from first principles — no frameworks doing the thinking for you.
Its strength is in modularity: every subsystem can survive independently.

Whoever picks this up next should:

Respect the wiring that already exists.

Extend, don’t overwrite.

Build it like a living system — one change at a time, eyes open.


